    "title": "Portland Trail Blazers TV Schedule",
    "text": "Learn how to watch or stream Portland Trail Blazers games during the 2025-26 season with the following local and national TV schedule. (Full NBA schedule available here.) This site may earn a commission on subscriptions purchased via this page. Friday, March 27 Time (UTC)Game / TV2:00 amDallas Mavericks vs Portland Trail BlazersNBA TV | A KFAA | H KUNP Sunday, March 29 Time (UTC)Game / TV10:00 pmWashington Wizards vs Portland Trail BlazersNBA League Pass | A MNMT | H KATU, KUNP Tuesday, March 31 Time (UTC)Game / TV3:00 amPortland Trail Blazers vs Los Angeles ClippersNBC, Peacock | A KUNP | H FDSN SC | NBA TV Canada Thursday, April 2 Time (UTC)Game / TV2:00 amNew Orleans Pelicans vs Portland Trail BlazersNBA League Pass | A GCSEN | H KUNP Monday, April 6 Time (UTC)Game / TV1:00 amPortland Trail Blazers vs Denver NuggetsNBA League Pass | A KUNP | H ALT, KTVD Wednesday, April 8 Time (UTC)Game / TV1:30 amPortland Trail Blazers vs San Antonio SpursESPN, ESPN Unlimited | A KUNP | H FDSN SW Friday, April 10 Time (UTC)Game / TV2:00 amLos Angeles Clippers vs Portland Trail BlazersNBA League Pass | A FDSN SC | H KUNP How to Watch Blazers Games in 2025 While he will likely not play much — if at all — this season, the return of Damian Lillard was the highlight of a Blazers offseason that also saw the addition of two-time NBA champion Jrue Holiday. Portland is set for 13 national TV games this season, considerably more than last year, but part of that is because NBC needs West Coast teams to fill its 11 PM ET windows on Tuesday nights. Indeed, six of Portland’s 13 national games are 11 PM ET windows on NBC. The Blazers are also set for streaming exclusive games on December 26 against the Clippers (Prime Video) and exactly one month later against the Celtics (Peacock), plus five games on NBA TV. Locally, 74 Blazers games are set to air on former Portland Univision affiliate KUNP — now an independent — with seven of those simulcast on ABC affiliate KATU (in addition to the national ABC games carried on that station). All of those local broadcasts are available to stream via the “BlazerVision” service. Direct-to-Subscriber Platforms Local games (BlazerVision): BlazerVision (in market only): Local coverage of Blazer games can be streamed with the BlazerVision service, which costs $120 for the full season. NBA League Pass (out-of-market only): All out-of-market locally televised games, plus NBA TV. Also available as a standalone purchase through Amazon Prime Video. National games (ESPN/ABC, NBC/Peacock and Prime Video): Peacock: All NBC Sports-produced games on the NBC broadcast network and Peacock. ESPN Unlimited: All ESPN-produced games on the ESPN cable networks and ABC. Disney+: Occasional simulcasts of ESPN-produced games. Amazon Prime Video: All Amazon-produced games on Prime Video, plus the ability to purchase NBA League Pass as an add-on. Cable and Streaming Bundles YouTube TV: All games on ESPN/ABC and the NBC broadcast network. Some Peacock-exclusive games will be available via NBCSN. (Peacock can also be purchased in full through YouTube Channels). Sponsored offer: Get $100 off YouTube TV ($20 off for 5 months) when you sign up today. New users only. Cancel anytime. Terms apply. Sling: All games on ESPN/ABC (ABC games will be on ESPN3); NBA League Pass available as an add-on. Fubo: All games on ESPN/ABC and the NBC broadcast network. DIRECTV (stream): All games on ESPN/ABC and the NBC broadcast network; NBA League Pass available as an add-on. Linear cable (ex. Dish Network, Xfinity, DIRECTV): All games on ESPN/ABC and the NBC broadcast network. Hulu + Live TV: All games on ESPN/ABC and the NBC broadcast network. In-Person See the Blazers in person at the arena formerly known as the Rose Garden (now the Moda Center) by purchasing tickets from Vivid Seats, SeatGeek or Gametime.",
